          <p>
            Sharing a splitter with neighbors is another option: split the cost of a gas machine among two or three households and take turns. Agree in advance on maintenance and storage. However you get one, plan your firewood workflow around the right tools; a good <a href="/best-chainsaw/">chainsaw</a> for cutting rounds, a splitter, and a hookaroon for moving pieces turn a punishing job into a manageable one. For general yard cleanup around the woodpile, see our <a href="/best-weed-eater/">weed eater guide</a>.
