          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you burn several cords a year, the Champion 27-Ton is the best balance of speed, vertical capability and price, with the Cub Cadet LS 27 for buyers who want dealer support and heavier construction. Fire pit and fireplace owners are better served by a quiet electric splitter such as the Boss ES7T20, and occasional users can get by with a manual hydraulic unit.
          </p>
